      "id": "2123604698695356510",
      "text": "When I’ve had a great run in the markets I start feeling anxiety.  I physically begin to note the stress and unease in my stomach.   It’s my early warning system telling me I’m about to fall on bad times.  \n\nIf it’s been a really good long run. Then I get really stressed. I fear it’s gonna be a bad, upsetting, depressing 6-9 months.\n\nWhen I’ve been bludgeoned for weeks or months I actually start feeling good.  I know that things are going to be looking up soon. \n\nI currently feel fantastic cause things are so grim.  Everything I bought today is underwater…. Everything i own has had a pretty nasty 1/2 year or so.  \n\nBut I’m starting to feel extremely optimistic.  I think its going to be an amazing 6-9 months ahead.",
